       VALUES (2, 13, 103, '2019-04-15', 1, 200);

-- Optionally, to force a join-duplication effect in Q2 one might add a (redundant) row in PRODUCT that still preserves the PRODUCT_ID primary key (for example, by using an indexed view or a join hint) so that the inner join in Q2 multiplies the SALES rows. This contrivance is only to illustrate that even though MIN and MAX are aggregate functions insensitive to duplicates, the order of operations (aggregation before join versus join before aggregation) makes Q1 and Q2 semantically different in principle.

