INSERT INTO SALES (PRODUCT_ID, SELLER_ID, BUYER_ID, SALE_DATE, QUANTITY, PRICE) 
VALUES (2, 20, NULL, '2020-01-02', 1, 200);

/* 
After these INSERTs, note that:
  • Q1’s subquery returns a set containing NULL (because of the IPHONE sale), so the condition
    1 NOT IN (NULL) evaluates to UNKNOWN; hence Q1 returns no rows.
  • In Q2, because the FROM clause forces a join on S8 records in the outer query, the problematic
    NULL from the IPHONE sale may be “left out” of the join’s effect for buyer 1 – so Q2 returns buyer 1.
This difference in output illustrates that Q1 and Q2 are not semantically equivalent.
*/

